# Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Two rules: a page is never cached, a hashed file under /assets always is.
#
# This file is not decoration. A route with no rule here gets the browser's own guess at how long
# a page stays fresh - and that guess is what broke the site: a reader opened /read/<id> once, the
# browser kept that day's index.html, the next deploy replaced the chunks it names, and the page
# then asked for files that no longer exist. Dead page until a hard refresh, while incognito
# (nothing cached) looked fine. Every address that can answer with index.html is listed below, and
# scripts/deploy-files.test.mjs fails when a route in src/lib/router.ts has no rule.
#
# A catch-all `/*` would not work: matching rules are MERGED, so `/*` would send `no-cache` along
# with `/assets/*`'s `immutable` and stop the chunks from caching at all.
#
# /sw.js is checked every visit too: an old worker must not keep answering for a new deploy.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  CDN-Cache-Control: no-store
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  CDN-Cache-Control: no-store
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  CDN-Cache-Control: no-store
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  CDN-Cache-Control: no-store
